==Old English==

===Etymology===
From an earlier form {{m|ang|hlāfweard}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*hlaibawarduz}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*hlaibaz||bread}} (whence {{m|ang|hlāf}}) + {{m|gem-pro|*warduz}} (whence {{m|ang|weard}}). Equivalent to {{m|en|loaf}} + {{m|en|ward}}. See also {{m|ang|hlǣfdīġe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhlɑːvord/|[ˈɬɑːvɔrd]|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=hlāford|m|hlāfordas}}

# [[lord]], master of servants
# male head of a household

